        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d0a63984-d0a8-5e1a-8242-392e13d81c3b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Ballarat Bitter\n- Companies: Ballarat Brewing Company\n- Places: Ballarat, Australia; Melbourne; Sydney\n- Concepts: bitter beer; top-fermented ale; pale ale\n- People: Ballarat Bertie; Ballarat Brewing Company director; advertising agency\n\nFacts:\n- In 1926, Ballarat Bertie was conceived on a train journey between Melbourne and Sydney by a Ballarat Brewing Company director and an advertising agency.\n- Ballarat Bitter is an Australian beer that was originally brewed in Ballarat, Australia by the Ballarat Brewing Company.\n- Ballarat Bitter has 4.9% alcohol by volume.\n- Ballarat Bitter is a bitter top-fermented ale.\n- Ballarat Bitter was traditionally sold in 750 ml longneck bottles, and its label featured Ballarat Bertie.\n- Bitter is a British style of pale ale that ranges in colour from gold to dark amber.\n- Bitter typically ranges in strength from 3% to 7% alcohol by volume.",
